<article class="env-lemma" id="092M">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/092M">Lemma <span data-tag="092M">15.106.12</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map such that $B \otimes _ A B \to B$ is flat. Then $\Omega _{B/A} = 0$, i.e., $B$ is formally unramified over $A$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $I \subset B \otimes _ A B$ be the kernel of the flat surjective map $B \otimes _ A B \to B$. Then $I$ is a pure ideal (Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/04PR" data-tag="04PR">10.108.1</a>), so $I^2 = I$ (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/04PS" data-tag="04PS">10.108.2</a>). Since $\Omega _{B/A} = I/I^2$ (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00RW" data-tag="00RW">10.131.13</a>) we obtain the vanishing. This means $B$ is formally unramified over $A$ by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00UO" data-tag="00UO">10.148.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>